# Sub-tick interpolation of the animated terrain. Row grammar and what the
# counts mean: see games/spyro-1/terrain-subtick-corpus.manifest.
#
# surface-swim: Spyro swims across the Sunrise Spring pond, so the animated
# water fills the lower frame. sheilas-alp: a second level, its waterfall and
# stream.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim.bk2 | 2000 |
sheilas-alp-sheila-water-invisible.bk2 | 4498 |
#
# Under --path terrain (the vertex-animation knob) both rows read VACUOUS: the
# two legs render the same present at every alpha, so no poly-animated vertex
# stands in either frame. Under --path terrain-tanim (the UV-scroll knob) both
# engage, 42894 px and 2076 px at alpha 0. Spyro 2 has no terrain manifest for
# the same reason on both knobs: shady-oasis-flame at V=848 and
# colossus-ice-skating at V=1120 each differ in 0 px at every alpha under both.
# The instrument is calibrated by Spyro 1, where the vertex-animation knob
# separates the legs by 53803 px at alpha 0.
